    "body": "The recovered native checkpoint first emits the correct “warm” but then emits “ir” where the next source token is “ b”, producing the prefix “You live in warmir”. Extend the offline target-free capture harness to load this qualified intermediate and authenticate 18 actual position-3/4 frames: that new failure plus the eight retained successful controls. Retain full bank provenance, BASE donor, Generate/U scores and physical-alias pools; attach labels after all captures. Compact token-ordered factors retain all4096 decompositions while preserving historical capture schemas. No serving policy or model parameter changes.\n\nIndependent saved arithmetic finds the desired source occurrence present and Prefix bins distinct from its rival in7/8lanes. Prefix already favours the target, but other BASE terms and U overturn it. The BASE bridge donor is from the wrong record while the final winner is from the expected record’s offset2; desiredoffset1 is available. Removing CopyU or using Generate-only does not fix the decision. All16 successful control frames remain correct. This narrows a native Context/read-to-emission credit question; it establishes no cursor requirement, global information loss, useful reply or capacity claim.\n\nValidation:11focusedtests/format/optimizedbuild at executed76e10b53f; exact final-head checks/review below. Actual18captures complete, full Rust seals and independent readerPASS:all73728G/U scores, bridge, Cue/Prefix relative bins/Q4/joint contributions, physical-alias pools and36saved-vector controls. Encoderstates remain authenticated witnesses, not independent encoder replay. Fullresult privately preserved/fresh-verified atHFdbc4f854a151987e1c398ce5c7216dca1b616678. Initial missing-feature wrapper and sealed output-cap failure retained separately; reportcap64->128MiB extension recorded before exactcap-only repair/freshretry. Actual replies remain8/512 and persistentgoalunmet.\n\nReferences #820.\n",
